# Local preview matches production

When changing this site, the local version must work the same way as the server. Do not treat `eleventy --serve` as the real site.

Production is a Cloudflare Worker (`worker/index.js`) in front of Eleventy output (`dist/`). The Worker rewrites public URLs and serves the API. Static Eleventy does neither, so links 404 and boards stay empty.

## How to run it

- Preview with `npm run serve` (`scripts/dev.mjs`): Eleventy watch plus `wrangler dev` on http://localhost:8080/, with local D1.
- `npm run serve:static` is only for markup that does not need routes or `/api`.

## Routing that must keep working

- `/leaderboards/<slug>/` is rewritten to `/leaderboards/_board/index.html`. The browser URL stays the slug.
- `/admin/leaderboards/<slug>/` is rewritten to `/admin/leaderboards/board.html`. The browser URL stays the slug.
- `/api/leaderboards/...` and `/api/admin/...` come from the Worker and D1, not from static files.

If an asset fetch redirects (`/file.html` → extensionless path), follow it inside the Worker and return the final body. Do not send that redirect to the browser.

## When you change the site

Verify the changed page through http://localhost:8080/ with the Worker running. Click the header links that the change affects. A page that only works in `eleventy --serve` is not done.
